A||||4||FieroMike||Kills: Eclipse/Sebring
Z||000000||FieroMike||04-08-99||12:09 PM||||Here are some of my kills in my 2-day old 1985 Fiero GT.  First kill was an old 280Z, that was fairly easy I thought.  I had an eclipse GS ('98) spot me and turn around and get next to me at a light.  He revved his gerbils a couple times and we took off, I had him through 1st, 2nd and 3rd up to about 90.  He was at least 3 car lengths behind me at the end.  A new Sebring also raced me and the same thing happend only he was about a car length and a half behind.  A real good race I had was an Eclipse GSX.  I had him through 1st and half of 2nd and then walked away from me. Those turbos are nice. I am going to get mine turbo charged as well so we will race again!  Any interesting kills? Take care.
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-08-99||05:43 PM||||Well, my 86.5 GT Automatic does 0-60 in 8.2s on a good day, and 9.2 on an average day, so I'm afraid the only "kills" I make is the occasional Rabbit. It's weird because when I just got the car (about 1.5 years ago), it felt a lot faster than it does today. I'm still convinced there's something wrong although a lot of people tell me those are normal acceleration times for the V6 Automatic... My old 85 GT Automatic was a lot faster though. It did 0-60 in about 7.5s.
Z||000002||Shaun41178||04-08-99||09:46 PM||||Those are Great kills FieroMike.  I am sure you had that GSX scared there for a second. I beat a 92 V8 Firebird and that guy was shocked I tell ya. That will teach those foreign cars not to mess with domestic power.  You can do a couple of mods to help improve the performance of your Fiero to beat that GSX next time you run into him.<p>Port the stock exhaust manifolds.  This can yield a 6-10 hp gain over stock.  I just finished with mine.  I couldn't "feel" a difference but I know that there was some hp gain.  Engine idles better now and and revs cleaner too.  My stock manifolds were restrictive as hell.  This is a good mod and parts to port should only cost you around $15.<p>Porting intake manifolds and heads can give about a 13-20 hp improvement.  You might not want to do major surgery on your car but if you have a spare ride then drive that around while you build up your fiero.<p>A nice cold air/high flow intake system, can give you about anotehr 5 hp. <br> <br>A lot of people are adding 1.6 rocker arms which can give you about 15 hp.  Or you could just add a cam but the engine would have to be removed to put in a higher lift cam.<p>Underdrive pulley will give a couple more horses.  Cost will be about $80<p>With these mods you can pick up roughly 30 or more hp.  This will surely be enought to kick that GSX's a$$<br>Once again great kills with the RS and Sebring
Z||000003||Pretender||04-09-99||01:40 AM||||The stock gsx has 210 hp..and runs the qtr. mile in 15.oo. 70 extra hp will do the job. have fun.
Z||000004||FieroMike||04-09-99||09:30 AM||||Shaun: Thanks for the info!! I was planning on having it re-bored and stroked, cams, street chip, and that Stage I turbo charger. I will consider porting and polishing the intake like you said also.<p>Cliff: That sounds slow to me, are you power braking on the start?  I heard the ADS chip will smooth out your transmission shifts in an auto and help out. (My '84 SE went 0-60 in 15.9 seconds!!!, automatic) Maybe you have a bad O2 sensor.<p>I just changed out all the vaccuum hoses and found a couple cracked ones and it runs a little better now, the only problem is my turn signals!!! (See Signal Problem!)<p>Has anyone ran a '98 or new v-6 grand am?
